blthtui (0.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Truncate device names by character instead of by byte, so non-ASCII names
    no longer render as garbage; non-printing characters are replaced rather
    than passed to the terminal.
  * Run Connect, Disconnect and Pair asynchronously. A blocking call could not
    answer our own pairing agent, so an outgoing pairing had no way to complete.
  * Show BlueZ's own error text instead of the errno string.
  * Update the device model from BlueZ signals rather than re-enumerating every
    object on each one: a 12s scan with 109 devices now issues one
    GetManagedObjects instead of roughly 480 round-trips.
  * Sort only on structural changes, so RSSI updates stop shuffling rows under
    the cursor; coalesce redraws to at most ten a second.
  * Add single-key actions (p pair, t trust, d details, r remove, s scan,
    / filter, o paired-only), a device details window with battery level and
    services, and an adapter picker when more than one adapter is present.
  * Detect the adapter disappearing at runtime and re-acquire it.
  * Unregister the pairing agent and stop discovery on exit.
  * Raise the device limit to 256 and say so when the list is full.

 -- Torn <automatorn@gmail.com>  Fri, 24 Jul 2026 06:56:06 +0300

blthtui (0.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release: adapter toggle, scan, connect/disconnect, pair/remove,
    interactive pairing agent, live signal-driven device list.

